.TH "SCMAGIMPORT" "1" "Sep 04, 2026" "7.4.0" "SeisComP"
.SH NAME
scmagimport \- SeisComP Documentation
.sp
\fBImports a foreign magnitude from a SCML event file into SeisComP.\fP
.SH DESCRIPTION
.sp
scmagimport imports a foreign \fI\%Magnitude\fP from a
\fI\%SCML\fP \fI\%Event\fP file into \fISeisComP\fP\&.
.sp
Processing steps performed:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP 1. 3
Extract the preferred \fI\%Origin\fP and magnitude from
the SCML event file.
.IP 2. 3
Check if the foreign magnitude is of a specific type, e.g., M(USGS).
.IP 3. 3
Use \fI\%scevent\fP to associate the origin to an SeisComP event. In this step
the foreign origin is send via HTTP POST to the \fI\%scevent\fP REST API
\fI/api/1/try\-to\-associate\fP which responds with an event ID if the association
was successful.
.IP 4. 3
Retrieve the event and the preferred origin from the local \fISeisComP\fP system.
.IP 5. 3
Copy the foreign magnitude to the preferred origin.
.IP 6. 3
Send the magnitude copy via a notifier message to \fI\%scmaster\fP\&.
.IP 7. 3
Let \fI\%scevent\fP decide whether the new magnitude becomes preferred.
.UNINDENT
.sp
Examples:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Read preferred origin and magnitude from \fI\%SCML\fP file
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.nf
.ft C
scmagimport \-i /path/to/seiscomp_event.xml
.ft P
.fi
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.IP \(bu 2
Use xalan and a XSLT file to convert \fI\%QuakeML\fP file to \fI\%SCML\fP and
pass it to the importer on stdin
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.nf
.ft C
xalan \-in /path/to/quakeml_event.xml \-xsl $SEISCOMP_ROOT/share/xml/0.14/quakeml__scml_0.14.xsl | scmagimport \-i \-
.ft P
.fi
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.SH COMMAND-LINE OPTIONS
.sp
\fBscmagimport [OPTIONS] source\fP
.SS Generic
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show help message.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-V, \-\-version
Show version information.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-\-config\-file file
The alternative module configuration file. When this option
is used, the module configuration is only read from the
given file and no other configuration stage is considered.
Therefore, all configuration including the definition of
plugins must be contained in that file or given along with
other command\-line options such as \-\-plugins.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-\-plugins arg
Load given plugins.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-D, \-\-daemon
Run as daemon. This means the application will fork itself
and doesn\(aqt need to be started with &.
.UNINDENT
.SS Verbosity
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-\-verbosity arg
